1. What is Force.com?
Force.com was the name of Salesforce's cloud application development platform.
It allowed developers to build custom business applications on Salesforce infrastructure without managing the underlying servers.
Today, the platform is generally referred to as the Salesforce Platform (Lightning Platform).

It provides two ways to develop applications:

1. Declarative development (Low-code / No-code)

Build applications using configuration and drag-and-drop tools without writing much code.

Examples:
- Object Manager
- Flow Builder
- Validation Rules
- Page Layouts
- Approval Processes

2. Programmatic development (Code-based)

Developers can write code to implement complex business requirements.

Examples:
- Apex
- Lightning Web Components (LWC)
- SOQL
- SOSL
- Salesforce APIs

